# RP2350 Touch LCD 2.8 SD/FAT hardware test

Read-only, on-board SDIO and FAT diagnostics. From the project root, configure
the `rp2350_touch_lcd_28` board and compile the test:

```sh
./configure --target arm-none-eabi --compiler arm-none-eabi-gcc --sdk pico-arm --board rp2350_touch_lcd_28 --runner none --build debug
./test --target --compile-only tests/boards/rp2350_touch_lcd_28
```

The test runner does not execute bare-metal images. Put the board in BOOTSEL
mode and flash the generated image with:

```sh
./flash --image out-target-arm-none-eabi/tests/rp2350-touch-lcd-28-sd-fat/rp2350-touch-lcd-28-sd-fat.uf2
```

The LCD retains the results. USB CDC receives the same lines when a terminal
is connected. The test identifies the card, reads raw sectors repeatedly,
compares unaligned and multiblock reads with single-block reads, checks the
last sector and out-of-range handling, mounts FAT read-only, queries capacity,
lists the root directory, and reads the first regular file twice. If the first
sector times out at the board's normal 25 MHz data clock, it retries at 4 MHz
to separate a data-clock problem from a basic transport failure.

This test never formats or writes to the SD card. A failure line names the
stage and `mm.fs` status. Leave the card inserted until the final summary.
